# ai-rules — mandatory coding standards

The standards library lives at `../../../Documents/GitHub/ai-rules/` (GitHub: `ssrkedu/ai-rules`).
It is also available in this workspace as `Documents/GitHub/ai-rules/`.
**Every code change must follow those rules.**

## Loading protocol

1. Open `RULES-INDEX.md` — never load the whole tree.
2. Classify the task (frontend only for this repo).
3. Open `frontend/00-index/frontend-rules-index.md` and pick **2–5** matching rule files from the task map.
4. Always load the frontend always-on set from `RULES-INDEX.md`:
   - `frontend/01-architecture/folder-structure-and-boundary-rules.md`
   - `frontend/05-quality/naming-and-file-rules.md`
   - `frontend/05-quality/forbidden-patterns-rules.md`
5. Add task-specific rules only when the work matches (examples):
   - Public site / trust + institution subdomains → `public-multi-site-architecture-rules.md`, `subdomain-site-context-rules.md`, `core-vs-feature-data-boundary-rules.md`
   - Components / templates → `component-and-template-rules.md`
   - API / HTTP / DTOs → `api-and-http-rules.md`, `api-url-and-endpoint-rules.md`
   - Styling / responsive → `scss-and-design-token-rules.md`, `accessibility-and-responsive-rules.md`
   - PrimeNG → `primeng-styling-rules.md`
6. For environment / deploy / hostname setup, also read `ai-rules/.cursor/skills/public-site-environment-setup.md`.

> Token discipline: typical tasks need **2–4 rule files**, not the entire library.

If `ai-rules/` is missing locally:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/ssrkedu/ai-rules.git ../../../Documents/GitHub/ai-rules
```
